{"name":"Carmine Red","hex":"#ff0038","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carmine red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purple-red pigment obtained from carmine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carmine_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carmine (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Carmine color is the general term for some deep red colors that are very slightly purplish but are generally slightly closer to pure red than the color crimson is. Some rubies have the color shown below as rich carmine. The deep dark red color shown at right as carmine is the color of the raw unprocessed pigment, but lighter, richer, or brighter colors are produced when the raw pigment is processed, some of which are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Carmine.png/330px-Carmine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmine_(color)","wikidata":"Q10296772"},{"title":"Carmine","blocks":[{"text":"Carmine – also called cochineal, cochineal extract, crimson lake, or carmine lake – is a pigment of a bright-red color obtained from the aluminium complex derived from carminic acid. Specific code names for the pigment include natural red 4, C.I. 75470, or E120. Carmine is also a general term for a particularly deep-red color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carmine.svg/330px-Carmine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmine","wikidata":"Q320617"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG/500px-Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG/1280px-Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG/500px-Carmine_skimmer_%28Orthemis_discolor%29_male_side.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carmine skimmer (male)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarmine_skimmer_(Orthemis_discolor)_male_side.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg/500px-Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg/1280px-Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg/500px-Dactylopius_coccus_%28Barlovento%29_04_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont